      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2011 New York Academy of Sciences.",
        "AbstractText": "We propose that predictive validity of tests for analgesia may be improved by looking to reinstate specific, innate behaviors suppressed by pain, e.g., burrowing, because effective plasma concentrations in the rat are closer to effective clinical plasma concentrations than those generally used in rodent reflex withdrawal assays."
